<title>BULGARIA: BULGARIA INTERNAL CREDIT FALLS 0.71 PCT IN WEEK.</title>
<headline>BULGARIA INTERNAL CREDIT FALLS 0.71 PCT IN WEEK.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian bank's internal credit</p>
<p>inched down to 1,163.6 billion levs on October 18 from 1,171.9</p>
<p>billion levs on October 11, preliminary central bank figures</p>
<p>showed.</p>
<p>Credit to government fell by 1.72 percent to 485.3 billion</p>
<p>levs, credit to state firms edged up 0.43 percent to 306.5</p>
<p>billion levs and lev-denominated credit to private firms fell</p>
<p>3.93 percent to 127.1 billion levs.</p>
<p> PERCENTAGE CHANGE	  OCT18-OCT11 OCT18-SEPT27 SEPT27-AUG30</p>
<p> Total internal credit	 -0.71	 -4.62	 +6.57</p>
<p> Credit to govt		  -1.72	 -2.16	 +4.75</p>
<p> Credit to state firms	 +0.43	 -5.52	 +7.39</p>
<p> Lev credit to private firms -3.93	 -5.15	 +1.30</p>
<p> NOMINAL (BILLION LEVS)	  OCT 18    OCT 11    SEPT 27</p>
<p> Total internal credit	  1,163.6   1,171.9    1,213.9</p>
<p> Credit to govt		     485.3     493.8	496.0</p>
<p> Credit to state firms	    306.5     305.2	324.4</p>
<p> Lev credit to private firms    127.1     132.3	134.0</p>
<p> Dlr credit to private firms	1.12	1.11	 1.13</p>
<p>(USD billion)</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, 359-2-84561</p>
</text>
